00:18:46.241 --> 00:18:48.818
You used to not to have to
worry about guns in schools,

00:18:48.818 --> 00:18:50.281
like, shooting people every minute.

00:18:50.281 --> 00:18:53.021
You used to not have to
worry about oil disappearing

00:18:53.021 --> 00:18:54.820
as we get close to
neutral oil prices, like,

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.596
you used to have to not
worry about everything.

00:18:56.596 --> 00:18:57.757
But you used to have to worry

00:18:57.757 --> 00:18:59.139
about the Soviet Union blowing you up.

00:18:59.139 --> 00:19:00.903
You used to have to worry about, like,

00:19:00.903 --> 00:19:03.251
not being able to cure
any version of cancer.

00:19:03.251 --> 00:19:05.817
Like, it's evolution, people.

00:19:05.817 --> 00:19:09.647
Sorry that music is not
the way it used to be.

00:19:09.647 --> 00:19:11.308
Sorry that it's evolved.

00:19:11.308 --> 00:19:14.233
You know, I don't see anybody
going crazy for bookstores

00:19:14.233 --> 00:19:16.927
and, you know, the bookstore
guy going up there like,

00:19:16.927 --> 00:19:19.271
(imitates crying noise)
Amazon came, sorry.

00:19:19.271 --> 00:19:23.067
Like, nobody's
super-duper-duper sad for cabs.

00:19:23.067 --> 00:19:24.612
The consumer's right.

00:19:24.612 --> 00:19:27.850
Not Common or Beyoncé.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:28.872
Got it?

00:19:28.872 --> 00:19:30.010
So it is what it is.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.507
Yes, it's important, yes,
music really matters.

00:19:32.507 --> 00:19:34.607
Yes, yes, guess what?

00:19:34.607 --> 00:19:36.104
When you were makin' all that money,

00:19:36.104 --> 00:19:37.545
music in 1955,

00:19:37.545 --> 00:19:39.506
the best baseball players in America

00:19:39.506 --> 00:19:40.726
and football players in America

00:19:40.726 --> 00:19:43.489
had jobs in the summer because
they didn't get paid a lot.

00:19:43.489 --> 00:19:44.509
But guess what happened?

00:19:44.509 --> 00:19:47.051
America decided they
really loved football,

00:19:47.051 --> 00:19:49.431
and that means that they
got more leverage over time,

00:19:49.431 --> 00:19:51.626
and now they get paid a lot of money,

00:19:51.626 --> 00:19:55.410
and they don't need side
jobs in the summer anymore.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:56.908
But maybe it flipped,

00:19:56.908 --> 00:19:59.904
and now you, musician,
actually have to hustle,

00:19:59.904 --> 00:20:01.923
and you maybe actually
have to like your fans,

00:20:01.923 --> 00:20:04.187
and you may actually have to take selfies,

00:20:04.187 --> 00:20:06.427
and you may actually
have to do live events,

00:20:06.427 --> 00:20:08.191
and you may have to do things.

00:20:08.191 --> 00:20:09.945
That's just the way it is.

00:20:09.945 --> 00:20:10.804
Period.

00:20:10.804 --> 00:20:12.151
Market dynamics.

00:20:12.151 --> 00:20:13.868
Everybody's affected by them.

00:20:13.868 --> 00:20:16.046
Always and forever.

00:20:17.514 --> 00:20:19.511
I want an article on that.

00:20:19.511 --> 00:20:21.751
Title it "Fuck You, Music Industry."

00:20:21.751 --> 00:20:22.738
(laughter)

00:20:22.738 --> 00:20:23.817
All right, something else, maybe.

00:20:23.817 --> 00:20:25.721
Question of the day.

00:20:25.721 --> 00:20:28.600
When have you been affected
by market conditions,

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:30.847
pro or con?

00:20:32.118 --> 00:20:34.636
You keep asking questions,

00:20:34.636 --> 00:20:36.552
I'll keep answering them.

00:20:36.552 --> 00:20:40.415
